This report covers footprinting the `networkwalks.com` domain using multiple Kali Linux tools (W2-PM1) and scanning my own local device with Zenmap (W2-PM5). One module covers the footprinting phase and the other covers the scanning phase, so together they show how an attacker moves from gathering public information to mapping what is running on a network. It is the Week 2 part of my ongoing internship at Networkwalks.

The footprinting commands were run in Kali Linux on 13 November 2026, and the scan was run from a Windows PC with Zenmap installed on 14 November 2026. Every step below includes the exact command used, the result I observed, a screenshot as evidence, and a short note on why the finding matters from an attacker's point of view.

